{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"cd7d4435-72d5-4048-a8b0-a5de386f21d9","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The server endpoint and client adapter have been updated to conform to the paginated response contract:\n\n- **[api_server.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-002_17776_1795169090521_baseline/api_server.py)**:\n  - Updated `handle_get_items(params: dict = None) -\u003e dict` to validate `page` (default `1`) and `page_size` (default `10`), returning `{\"status\": 400, \"error\": {\"code\": \"INVALID_PAGINATION\", \"message\": \"page and page_size must be \u003e= 1\"}}` when either parameter is `\u003c 1`.\n  - Sliced `DATABASE_ITEMS` according to the requested page and computed `pagination` metadata (`page`, `page_size`, `total_items`, `total_pages`, `has_next`, `has_prev`), returning an empty `items` list with valid metadata when `page \u003e total_pages`.\n  - Preserved `handle_health_check()` unchanged.\n- **[api_client.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-002_17776_1795169090521_baseline/api_client.py)**:\n  - Updated `ApiClient.fetch_items_page` to detect error responses (`status \u003e= 400` or `\"error\"` dictionary) and raise `ApiError` with the server's error message.\n  - Parsed `items` into `Item` dataclass instances and mapped `pagination` metadata into a `PaginatedResult` instance, handling empty out-of-range pages gracefully.\n- **[test_visible.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-002_17776_1795169090521_baseline/tests/test_visible.py)**:\n  - Added unit tests covering default pagination, multi-page boundary navigation, out-of-range pages, invalid pagination parameters, and client `ApiError` handling.\n","duration_seconds":82.8944375,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":39144,"output_tokens":3616,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":158208,"total_tokens":42760}}}
